{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerFactorial"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.qInt_one_eq_natCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.qInt_one_eq_natCast","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.lean#L84-L88","doc":"**q→1 degeneration:** `[n]_1 = n`. The candidate q-difference base operator recovers\nthe classical integer coefficient in the classical limit, so `D_q → d/dz` as `q → 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.jackson_monomial_numerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.jackson_monomial_numerator","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.lean#L76-L82","doc":"**The Jackson q-derivative names the quantum integer `[n]_q`** (over a `Field`,\nreusing the corpus `QOU.MathlibExt.qInt`): `(q·z)^n − z^n = [n]_q · (q−1) · z^n`. Contrast the classical\n`d/dz (z^n) = n·z^{n−1}` (`n` is q-free); here the coefficient is `[n]_q`, so the base\noperator is genuinely non-classical — the mechanism the C1 kernel needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.jackson_monomial_numerator_commRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.jackson_monomial_numerator_commRing","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.lean#L65-L74","doc":"**The cleared Jackson q-derivative on a monomial** (over any `CommRing`).\n`(q·z)^n − z^n = (∑_{i<n} q^i)·(q−1)·z^n`. The bracket `∑_{i<n} q^i` is the quantum\ninteger `[n]_q`; dividing by the Jackson denominator `(q−1)z` gives\n`D_q(z^n) = [n]_q · z^{n−1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.qShift_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.qShift_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.lean#L60-L63","doc":"`σ_q` sends the monomial `w ↦ w^n` to `z ↦ q^n · z^n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.qShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.qShift","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDiffProlongationBaseOperator.lean#L56-L58","doc":"**The base q-dilation** `σ_q f = z ↦ f(q·z)` — the candidate base operator whose\njet-tower lift would be the sought prolongation `D_q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}